    "lawCode": "Amd §517-c, R & SS L",
    "lawSection": "Retirement and Social Security Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9327\n\nSPONSOR: BAILEY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the retirement and social security law, in relation to\nallowing certain members of the New York city police pension fund to\nborrow from contributions\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis bill relates to the restoration of rights for certain members of\nthe New York City police pension fund to borrow from their contributions\nto the fund.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis bill amends Section 517(c) of the retirement and social security\nlaw to allow Tier 3, Tier 3 Revised, and Tier 3 Enhanced members of the\nNew York City Police Pension Fund (\"PPF\") as of Januaryl, 2018 to borrow\nfrom contributions made to that fund under conditions consistent with\nexisting law that allows members of the State and Local Employee Retire-\nment System to do the same.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nCurrently, Tier 3 New York City PPF members are prohibited from borrow-\ning from their contributions pursuant to the Retirement and Social Secu-\nrity Law (\"RSSL\") § 517 (c). Tier 1 and 2members of the PPF are permit-\nted to borrow from their contributions. Other state and local employees\nsubject to RSSL Article 14, including those covered by the New York\nState and Local Employees' Retirement System, the New York State Employ-\nees Retirement System, the New York State Police and Fire Retirement\nSystem, the New York State Teachers' Retirement System, the New York\nCity Teachers' Retirement System, the New York City Board of Education\nRetirement System and certain members of the New York City Employees'\nRetirement System, are also permitted to borrow, pursuant to RSSL §§\n517, 517-b, and 517-c. The ability to take pension loans has long been a\nbenefit for police officers who use these loans to assist with educa-\ntional expenses, a down payment on a mortgage, or another vital need.\nThe proposed legislation would restore this important right in a manner\nthat is consistent with the rights available to police officers and\nother public employees throughout New York City and New York State.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2019: S5906B - Referred to Civil Service & Pensions\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nSee bill.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
